---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import BlogPosts from "../../components/BlogPosts.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Me" description="Meet Ava Celeste — Richmond mature escort.">
  <section class="intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Meet</p>
    <h1 class="accent-text">Ava Celeste</h1>
    <p class="drop-cap">
      A true Bohemian spirit in business casual — Brooks Brothers on top, Lise Charmel underneath. A
      somewhat-cynical eccentric who naively believes in truth, beauty, freedom, and love, understanding
      that all of those things take a variety of forms. Techy enough to hand-code my website in HTML if I
      <em>really</em> had to — but I do my best thinking with a fountain pen and Clairefontaine paper,
      sustained by matcha from a 300-year-old Japanese company.
    </p>
    <p class="eyebrow">Richmond mature escort</p>
    <p>
      A mix of free spirit and Type A. The perfect analog companion for a successful man who yearns to
      turn off his digital life to enjoy his actual one.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Curiosity fuels me</h2>
    <p>
      A large part of my creativity is fueled by boundless curiosity about everything — I want to know
      why and how, which explains a lot of my travels (and unfortunately, some squirrel-brain tendencies).
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm genuine, intensely focused, a fast learner, a deep thinker, intuitive. I love learning and
      research to a fault. I'm an avid listener, and I retain quite a bit of what you tell me — I ask why
      because I genuinely want to know.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Freedom by design</h2>
    <p>
      I knew very early in life I didn't want to be a soccer mom or an office drone. No kids, never
      married, never part of the corporate world. I've not only taken the road less traveled — I've left
      that road entirely and gone into the bush. You've likely not met anyone quite like me.
    </p>
    <p>I do not suffer life FOMO.</p>
    <p>
      My freedom has meant I've lived life somewhat backwards: I spent my younger years living and
      exploring, and only recently figured out what I wanted to do with myself. You've probably taken the
      more traditional route, felt stifled, and decided it's time to start living.
    </p>
    <p>So here we are, meeting in the middle of our lives (like Benjamin Button and Daisy Fuller).</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Physically</h2>
    <ul class="stats-list">
      <li>5'8", 34C — natural and in place</li>
      <li>Real — nails, hair, eyelashes (nails buffed, not polished; toes w/ red polish)</li>
      <li>Jewelry — tend not to wear much beyond Mikimoto pearls</li>
      <li>Gen X — so I'll get all your references</li>
      <li>Avid Pilates student and beginner weight-lifter — firm, with curves</li>
      <li>Very smooth skin, a few scars from life, no stretch marks</li>
      <li>Believes that <em>feels</em> good and <em>looks</em> good shouldn't be different things</li>
      <li>I tend not to dress for attention, I don't feel the need</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>My personality, as quiz results</h2>
    <ul class="quiz-list">
      <li><strong>Myers-Briggs:</strong> INFJ</li>
      <li><strong>Clifton Strengths (Top 3):</strong> Intellection, Restorative, Adaptability</li>
      <li><strong>Enneagram Type:</strong> 5 – The Investigator</li>
      <li><strong>Big Five Model:</strong> Openness</li>
      <li><strong>Alphabet Type:</strong> C</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      All of these tests essentially say the same thing about me in different ways. I listen and think,
      I explore, I'm adaptable and curious, with a tendency to live in my head [and over-think].
    </p>
    <p>
      Importantly for you, I have the power of restoration. I like to leave something better than I found
      it. I like the idea of being a gift to each other's lives.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Humor: witty is just one piece of the whole</h2>
    <p>
      Hopefully you can detect some of my humor through the screen. If you think something I say sounds
      ridiculous, it's likely meant to <em>be</em> ridiculous. I can quote quite a lot of Monty Python, if
      that helps.
    </p>
    <p>
      It's not just talented performers or great comedy movies. I have a keen sense of life's absurdities,
      and have been through enough to have earned a sense of gallows humor, too. I know how and when to
      laugh at myself.
    </p>
    <p>
      I enjoy silliness and irony and slapstick and Dad jokes and pointed social satire. Cruelty is
      probably the only thing that never makes me laugh. Malice isn't funny; banana peels are.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The way you do anything is how you do everything</h2>
    <p>
      My super-powers and super-weaknesses are all exactly the same things. Hyper-focus. Compassion.
      Honesty. Perfectionism. The ability to see multiple perspectives. Always noticing every detail. A
      robust sense of humor. Thrill-seeker. Explorer. All-natural. Physically sensitive. Self-aware.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="blog">
    <h2>Blog posts where I over-think in public</h2>
    <BlogPosts variant="card" limit={3} />
    <p class="wip-note">
      Works in progress: <em>Curiosity</em>, <em>The Attention Economy</em>, <em>Choice</em> — more soon.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>No regrets — anti-FOMO</h2>
    <p>
      I've, presumably, lived half my life. It's been a good half, and most of my regrets revolve around
      not beginning something sooner.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you believe this is the one life you get — no second chances, no do-overs — then live with as
      few regrets as possible.
    </p>
    <p>If we're both here, why not go for it?</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .intro { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .intro h1 { font-size: 3rem; margin: 0.25rem 0 1rem; }
  .eyebrow {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  .stats-list, .quiz-list { padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .stats-list li, .quiz-list li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  .wip-note { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); }
</style>
